  "provider_query": "Find the public X status from OpenAI that announces GPT-4",
  "answer": "The official OpenAI account post announcing GPT-4 is:\n\n**https://x.com/OpenAI/status/1635687373060317185**  \n@OpenAI · 14 Mar 2023, 17:00 UTC  \n“Announcing GPT-4, a large multimodal model, with our best-ever results on capabilities and alignment: https://openai.com/product/gpt-4”  \n(~59.7K likes, ~16K reposts; includes video) [web:0]\n\nRelated public posts from the same launch (14 Mar 2023):\n\n1. **https://x.com/gdb/status/1635687252616679426** — Greg Brockman (@gdb), ~17:00 UTC: “We’re releasing GPT-4 — a large multimodal model (image & text in, text out)…” linking to the research post. [web:3]\n2. **https://x.com/sama/status/1635687853324902401** — Sam Altman (@sama), ~17:02 UTC: “here is GPT-4, our most capable and aligned model yet. it is available today in our API (with a waitlist) and in ChatGPT+.” [web:12]\n3. **https://x.com/miramurati/status/1635688069692293121** — Mira Murati (@miramurati), ~17:03 UTC: “Unveiling GPT-4 — our large multimodal model…” [web:4]\n4. **https://x.com/npew/status/1635687624047489024** — Peter Welinder (@npew), ~17:01 UTC: “GPT-4 is here: our smartest and most reliable model yet!” [web:14]\n5. **https://x.com/verge/status/1635688829792268307** — The Verge (@verge), ~17:06 UTC: coverage of the OpenAI GPT-4 announcement. [web:2]\n6. **https://x.com/rowancheung/status/1635690962973339672** (thread) — Rowan Cheung, ~17:14 UTC: “OpenAI just launched GPT-4.” [web:6]\n7. **https://x.com/Dexerto/status/1635691060511879181** — Dexerto, ~17:15 UTC: “Open AI released GPT-4 today.” [web:19]\n\nThe canonical company announcement is the @OpenAI status above.",
